            <div xml:id="d773">

                <pb facs="0577" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.48/1407: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-25T19:00:00-05:00">January 25, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. Your 48, January 23, 5 p.m. For your information. The Department has amended
                    the text of the first sentence of your statement, contained in the telegram
                    under reference, to read as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The hostilities are driving huge numbers of Chinese from their homes, in
                            cities and villages and on farms. Fleeing from danger, <pb facs="0578"
                                n="574" xml:id="pg574"/> very many of these people become refugees
                            and are in need of shelter, food, clothing, and medical aid.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
